[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186124461 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" "question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" "question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" "question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/id #uuid "57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130710" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+xy+2x+y$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1)$, can be found by computing $∇f(1,-1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+xy+2x+y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+xy+2x+y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(2x+y+2)\\text{ }i+(-2y+x+1)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =(2(1)+(-1)+2)\\text{ }i+(-2(-1)+1+1)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =3\\,i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(1,-1)}{‖∇f(1,-1)‖} & =\\frac{3\\,i+4\\,j}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=\\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8" "answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" "answer-98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78" "answer-298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa" "answer-872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8" :answer/id #uuid "35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" :answer/id #uuid "2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78" :answer/id #uuid "98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(4\\,i-3\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa" :answer/id #uuid "298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2" :answer/id #uuid "872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/id #uuid "728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/math-academy-id "q-129910" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy+8y$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-2)$, can be found by computing $∇f(2,-2).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(2,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy+8y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy+8y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(2x-2y)\\text{ }i+(2y-2x+8)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =(2(2)-2(-2))\\text{ }i+(2(-2)-2(2)+8)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =8\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(2,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(2,-2)}{‖∇f(2,-2)‖} & =\\frac{8\\,i}{\\sqrt{{8}^{2}}}=i\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/id #uuid "3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769" "answer-ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64" "answer-a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5" "answer-500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49" "answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769" :answer/id #uuid "f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64" :answer/id #uuid "ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\,i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5" :answer/id #uuid "a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49" :answer/id #uuid "500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2\\,i-j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c" :answer/id #uuid "0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/id #uuid "22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71384" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-xy$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-1)$, can be found by computing $∇f(2,-1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-xy)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-xy)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{x+y}-y)\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{x+y}-x)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & =(\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}-(-1))\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}-2)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =2i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(2,-1)}{‖∇f(2,-1)‖} & =\\frac{2i-j}{\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2i-j}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73" "answer-95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b" "answer-032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52" "answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" "answer-7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73" :answer/id #uuid "db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b" :answer/id #uuid "95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(i+2j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52" :answer/id #uuid "032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2i+j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" :answer/id #uuid "b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2i-j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128" :answer/id #uuid "7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/id #uuid "b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71382" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1)$, can be found by computing $∇f(1,-1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{ }i+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\text{ }i+\\frac{2(-1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(1,-1)}{‖∇f(1,-1)‖} & =\\frac{i-j}{\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{i-j}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" :answer-field/choices ["answer-df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7" "answer-3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb" "answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" "answer-2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f" "answer-118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7" :answer/id #uuid "df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb" :answer/id #uuid "3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" :answer/id #uuid "389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f" :answer/id #uuid "2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(i-j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146" :answer/id #uuid "118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124463 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/id #uuid "ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131118" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2},$ find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,-2,0).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(2x+{x}^{2}yz){e}^{xyz}\\,i+({x}^{3}z{e}^{xyz}+2y)\\,j+{x}^{3}y{e}^{xyz}\\,k \\\\ ∇f(1,-2,0) & =(2(1)+({1}^{2})(-2)(0)){e}^{1(-2)(0)}\\,i+(({1}^{3})(0){e}^{1(-2)(0)}+2(-2))\\,j+({1}^{3})(-2){e}^{1(-2)(0)}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-4\\,j-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2\\,i-4\\,j-2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/id #uuid "22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6" "answer-7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0" "answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" "answer-f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805" "answer-ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6" :answer/id #uuid "55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0" :answer/id #uuid "7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" :answer/id #uuid "6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-4\\,j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805" :answer/id #uuid "f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,i-j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d" :answer/id #uuid "ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j+4\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125740 :tutorial/content "The same property holds true in the case of three or more variables. In general, if $f$ is a differentiable real-valued function of $n$ variables, $\\mathbf y$ is a point in the domain of $f,$ and if  the  gradient vector is nonzero, i.e., \n\n$$\n\\nabla f (\\mathbf y)= \\left \\langle f_{x_1}(\\mathbf y), f_{x_2}(\\mathbf y), \\cdots, f_{x_n}(\\mathbf y)\\right \\rangle \\neq \\mathbf 0,\n$$\n\nthen we have the following result:\n\n*$\\nabla f (\\mathbf y)$ is a normal vector to the level surface $f(x_1,x_2, \\cdots, x_n) =f(\\mathbf y)$ at $\\mathbf y.$*\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the function  \n\n$$\nw = f (x, y, z)= \\dfrac 1 2\\left(x^2 + y^2 + z^2-1\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nThe level surface corresponding to $w=0$ is the sphere $\\mathcal S$ with equation $x^2 + y^2 +z^2 =1.$ \n\nThe point $P(0,0,1)$ lies on $\\mathcal S.$ Computing $\\nabla f(0,0,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(x,y,z) &= \\langle f_x, \\: f_y, \\:f_z\\rangle \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac12\\langle2x, \\: 2y, \\: 2z\\rangle\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\langle x, \\: y, \\: z\\rangle\\\\[10pt]\n\n\\nabla f(0,0,1) &= \\langle 0,\\: 0,\\: 1 \\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow clearly, $\\nabla f (0,0, 1)$ is perpendicular to $\\mathcal S$ at the point $(0,0,1).$\n\n![](images/88/88bf25de31ae3318379865cdf2590c15216cb984cbf3948f975caa47317be664.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/id #uuid "57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e"] ["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130710"] ["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+xy+2x+y$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1).$"] ["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1)$, can be found by computing $∇f(1,-1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+xy+2x+y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+xy+2x+y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(2x+y+2)\\text{ }i+(-2y+x+1)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =(2(1)+(-1)+2)\\text{ }i+(-2(-1)+1+1)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =3\\,i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(1,-1)}{‖∇f(1,-1)‖} & =\\frac{3\\,i+4\\,j}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=\\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e"] ["answer-35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8" :answer/id #uuid "35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8"] ["answer-35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8" :answer/value "-j"] ["answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" :answer/id #uuid "2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba"] ["answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,j)"] ["answer-98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78" :answer/id #uuid "98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78"] ["answer-98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(4\\,i-3\\,j)"] ["answer-298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa" :answer/id #uuid "298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa"] ["answer-298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+\\,j)"] ["answer-872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2" :answer/id #uuid "872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2"] ["answer-872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2" :answer/value "i"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/correct "answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/choices "answer-35d25c51-dfcd-51fc-a6c5-cfba7faf93c8"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/choices "answer-2409f922-d37b-52c8-b658-31fce748e2ba"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/choices "answer-98cc5321-69a6-5c55-bb35-e3e0990fcf78"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/choices "answer-298df80d-8ba7-5971-a5be-5f47ba173aaa"] ["answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e" :answer-field/choices "answer-872f1d91-3616-5885-a3fb-55ee0f8eeaa2"] ["question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4b0633ad-b5b5-5018-885c-c9378c08481e"] [17592186124461 :knowledge-point/questions "question-57b49f13-0a2a-5f52-9cc1-6ee2c2a0903e"] ["question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/id #uuid "728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03"] ["question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/math-academy-id "q-129910"] ["question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy+8y$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-2).$"] ["question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-2)$, can be found by computing $∇f(2,-2).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(2,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy+8y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2xy+8y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(2x-2y)\\text{ }i+(2y-2x+8)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =(2(2)-2(-2))\\text{ }i+(2(-2)-2(2)+8)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =8\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(2,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(2,-2)}{‖∇f(2,-2)‖} & =\\frac{8\\,i}{\\sqrt{{8}^{2}}}=i\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/id #uuid "3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253"] ["answer-f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769" :answer/id #uuid "f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769"] ["answer-f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769" :answer/value "-j"] ["answer-ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64" :answer/id #uuid "ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64"] ["answer-ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64" :answer/value "\\,i+j"] ["answer-a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5" :answer/id #uuid "a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5"] ["answer-a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j)"] ["answer-500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49" :answer/id #uuid "500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49"] ["answer-500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2\\,i-j)"] ["answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c" :answer/id #uuid "0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c"] ["answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c" :answer/value "i"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/correct "answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/choices "answer-f5a5d6a5-c65c-525b-a225-edbf38f69769"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/choices "answer-ff481663-9345-5ec5-a52f-457045dd7b64"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/choices "answer-a4881f5d-4c74-5ce0-a573-e88708e1aff5"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/choices "answer-500271bb-f899-5f15-8b03-04f59f53cf49"] ["answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253" :answer-field/choices "answer-0369593a-3f7e-5fb8-b29d-ae4a507e9a3c"] ["question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3867fe6c-1021-55a8-96ee-bf07851c7253"] [17592186124461 :knowledge-point/questions "question-728b8816-964d-5b2c-b1e2-928105ec3a03"] ["question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/id #uuid "22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b"] ["question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71384"] ["question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-xy$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-1).$"] ["question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(2,-1)$, can be found by computing $∇f(2,-1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-xy)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)-xy)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{x+y}-y)\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{x+y}-x)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & =(\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}-(-1))\\text{ }i+(\\frac{1}{2+(-1)}-2)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =2i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(2,-1)}{‖∇f(2,-1)‖} & =\\frac{2i-j}{\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2i-j}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6"] ["answer-db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73" :answer/id #uuid "db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73"] ["answer-db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73" :answer/value "-j"] ["answer-95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b" :answer/id #uuid "95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b"] ["answer-95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(i+2j)"] ["answer-032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52" :answer/id #uuid "032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52"] ["answer-032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2i+j)"] ["answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" :answer/id #uuid "b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c"] ["answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}(2i-j)"] ["answer-7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128" :answer/id #uuid "7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128"] ["answer-7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128" :answer/value "i"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/correct "answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-db7d5bf9-08cf-5bfc-bf08-aa6568808a73"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-95e2877d-3409-5570-b9e1-5b49b7a7040b"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-032c2757-efa9-5509-bcca-3daaadba1e52"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-b333ea2a-2c2c-5da6-9892-bd490c4e153c"] ["answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6" :answer-field/choices "answer-7d92482e-2f72-52fc-9059-c074d418b128"] ["question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d6670180-2250-5bbf-88e5-1ac41691a6d6"] [17592186124461 :knowledge-point/questions "question-22134247-39ad-5cd2-bebd-e89dbb4b1f1b"] ["question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/id #uuid "b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b"] ["question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71382"] ["question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/problem "Find a unit normal vector to the level curve of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1).$"] ["question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(1,-1)$, can be found by computing $∇f(1,-1).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{ }i+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\text{ }i+\\frac{2(-1)}{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $∇f(1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∇f(1,-1)}{‖∇f(1,-1)‖} & =\\frac{i-j}{\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{i-j}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3"] ["answer-df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7" :answer/id #uuid "df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7"] ["answer-df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7" :answer/value "-j"] ["answer-3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb" :answer/id #uuid "3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb"] ["answer-3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i+j)"] ["answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" :answer/id #uuid "389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af"] ["answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af" :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(i-j)"] ["answer-2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f" :answer/id #uuid "2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f"] ["answer-2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f" :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(i-j)"] ["answer-118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146" :answer/id #uuid "118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146"] ["answer-118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146" :answer/value "i"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/correct "answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/choices "answer-df593630-ccc7-5531-a86e-3a99b075f8f7"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/choices "answer-3bb26b51-4f96-5040-bc73-852a85ed3afb"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/choices "answer-389b4032-f597-5b8b-9fd1-e1313e2896af"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/choices "answer-2d9fb5d0-4e4d-56ab-80c9-093d2e1af62f"] ["answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3" :answer-field/choices "answer-118335a9-3f2f-5e77-8049-daf71b5ec146"] ["question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c522a1b1-6aa4-5c25-9679-9d75080dc4e3"] [17592186124461 :knowledge-point/questions "question-b7d1bf90-ec36-5fa3-9648-a21ed4abb91b"] ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/id #uuid "ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b"] ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131118"] ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2},$ find a vector that's perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0).$"] ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/worked-solution "A normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0)$ can be found by computing \n$∇f(1,-2,0).$ \n\nSo, we first find the gradient and evaluate it at $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}{e}^{xyz}+{y}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(2x+{x}^{2}yz){e}^{xyz}\\,i+({x}^{3}z{e}^{xyz}+2y)\\,j+{x}^{3}y{e}^{xyz}\\,k \\\\ ∇f(1,-2,0) & =(2(1)+({1}^{2})(-2)(0)){e}^{1(-2)(0)}\\,i+(({1}^{3})(0){e}^{1(-2)(0)}+2(-2))\\,j+({1}^{3})(-2){e}^{1(-2)(0)}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\,i-4\\,j-2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2\\,i-4\\,j-2\\,k$ is perpendicular to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(1,-2,0).$"] ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/id #uuid "22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5"] ["answer-55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6" :answer/id #uuid "55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6"] ["answer-55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6" :answer/value "2\\,i-2\\,j+k"] ["answer-7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0" :answer/id #uuid "7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0"] ["answer-7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0" :answer/value "2\\,i-2\\,k"] ["answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" :answer/id #uuid "6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf"] ["answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf" :answer/value "2\\,i-4\\,j-2\\,k"] ["answer-f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805" :answer/id #uuid "f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805"] ["answer-f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805" :answer/value "4\\,i-j-2\\,k"] ["answer-ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d" :answer/id #uuid "ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d"] ["answer-ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d" :answer/value "j+4\\,k"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/correct "answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/choices "answer-55dd2830-6432-52c0-a771-384b6364ede6"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/choices "answer-7a765b73-bb6d-588d-b943-9033158431d0"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/choices "answer-6a6833e3-d101-5239-8525-af4ff8b4fdaf"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/choices "answer-f762dc04-a888-5706-8878-b795fb0dc805"] ["answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5" :answer-field/choices "answer-ca7234d8-3e14-5c71-b5b0-e92152c1bf9d"] ["question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-22190f85-7ea5-5d9f-80dd-195c9acabba5"] [17592186124463 :knowledge-point/questions "question-ff3d7f48-7543-5dd7-9bd4-9af3c29d885b"] [17592186125740 :tutorial/content "The same property holds true in the case of three or more variables. In general, if $f$ is a differentiable real-valued function of $n$ variables, $\\mathbf y$ is a point in the domain of $f,$ and if  the  gradient vector is nonzero, i.e., \n\n$$\n\\nabla f (\\mathbf y)= \\left \\langle f_{x_1}(\\mathbf y), f_{x_2}(\\mathbf y), \\cdots, f_{x_n}(\\mathbf y)\\right \\rangle \\neq \\mathbf 0,\n$$\n\nthen we have the following result:\n\n*$\\nabla f (\\mathbf y)$ is a normal vector to the level surface $f(x_1,x_2, \\cdots, x_n) =f(\\mathbf y)$ at $\\mathbf y.$*\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the function  \n\n$$\nw = f (x, y, z)= \\dfrac 1 2\\left(x^2 + y^2 + z^2-1\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nThe level surface corresponding to $w=0$ is the sphere $\\mathcal S$ with equation $x^2 + y^2 +z^2 =1.$ \n\nThe point $P(0,0,1)$ lies on $\\mathcal S.$ Computing $\\nabla f(0,0,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\nabla f(x,y,z) &= \\langle f_x, \\: f_y, \\:f_z\\rangle \\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac12\\langle2x, \\: 2y, \\: 2z\\rangle\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\langle x, \\: y, \\: z\\rangle\\\\[10pt]\n\n\\nabla f(0,0,1) &= \\langle 0,\\: 0,\\: 1 \\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow clearly, $\\nabla f (0,0, 1)$ is perpendicular to $\\mathcal S$ at the point $(0,0,1).$\n\n![](images/88/88bf25de31ae3318379865cdf2590c15216cb984cbf3948f975caa47317be664.png)"]] "retractions" [[17592186125740 :tutorial/content "The same property holds true in the case of three or more variables. In general, if $f$ is a differentiable real-valued function of $n$ variables, $\\mathbf y$ is a point in the domain of $f,$ and if  the  gradient vector is nonzero, i.e., \n\n$$\n\\nabla f (\\mathbf y)= \\left \\langle f_{x_1}(\\mathbf y), f_{x_2}(\\mathbf y), \\cdots, f_{x_n}(\\mathbf y)\\right \\rangle \\neq \\mathbf 0,\n$$\n\nthen we have the following result:\n\n*$\\nabla f (\\mathbf y)$ is a normal vector to the level surface $f(x_1,x_2, \\cdots, x_n) =f(\\mathbf y)$ at $\\mathbf y.$*\n\nTo illustrate, let's consider the function  \n\n$$\nw = f (x, y, z)= \\dfrac 1 2\\left(x^2 + y^2 + z^2-1\\right).\n$$\n\n \n\nThe level surface corresponding to $w=0$ is the sphere $\\mathcal S$ with equation $x^2 + y^2 +z^2 =1.$ \n\nThe point $P(0,0,1)$ lies on $\\mathcal S.$ Computing $\\nabla f(0,0,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\nabla f(x,y,z) &= \\langle f_x, \\: f_y, \\:f_z\\rangle \\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac12\\langle2x, \\: 2y, \\: 2z\\rangle\\[5pt]\n&= \\langle x, \\: y, \\: z\\rangle\\[10pt]\n\n\\nabla f(0,0,1) &= \\langle 0,\\: 0,\\: 1 \\rangle.\n}\n$$\n\nNow clearly, $\\nabla f (0,0, 1)$ is perpendicular to $\\mathcal S$ at the point $(0,0,1).$\n\n![](images/88/88bf25de31ae3318379865cdf2590c15216cb984cbf3948f975caa47317be664.png)"]]}]